  "oauth_settings_contract": {
    "note": "Thinking-level contract for OAuth channels whose client surface is the codex (Responses) protocol. The antigravity lane is served to Codex clients, whose built-in thinking capability for these models is the codex family default low/medium/high (sdk/cliproxy/service_models.go buildConfiguredModelInfo), while the same catalog publishes the gemini-4-*-xhigh slugs. Without a declaration an xhigh turn had no enforceable bound on the lane. The declaration stays out of oauth_settings on purpose: that mapping is projected verbatim into oauth.settings and must keep holding only what the gateway serves. The fork build v8.0.79+agy-effort clamps an unsupported level there instead of forwarding it to an upstream that silently substitutes another model (2026-11-17 flash-high -> flash-n). Only the anthropic (Claude) models of the lane consume it: the Gemini models are user-defined and keep their own handling.",
    "channels": {
      "antigravity": {
        "thinking-levels": ["low", "medium", "high"]
      }
    }
  },
